# Eggnog

Based on [A Luxurious and Strong Eggnog Recipe](https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/voraciously/wp/2019/12/11/a-luxurious-and-strong-eggnog-recipe-to-sustain-you-through-this-holiday-season-and-many-more) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20210514174134/https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/voraciously/wp/2019/12/11/a-luxurious-and-strong-eggnog-recipe-to-sustain-you-through-this-holiday-season-and-many-more)) in the Washington Post

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 6 large [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" }
- [ ] 2 cups (8 ounces) [confectioners’ sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 cup [light rum]{ ing="light-rum" }
- [ ] 1 quart [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" } or half-and-half
- [ ] 1 cup [cognac or Asbach brandy]{ ing="cognac-or-asbach-brandy" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [orange liqueur]{ ing="orange-liqueur" }, such as Grand Marnier or Cointreau
- [ ] Freshly [grated nutmeg]{ ing="grated-nutmeg" }, for garnish

## Recipe

1. In a large bowl, beat the [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" } with a whisk until light in color. Gradually whisk in the [confectioners’ sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" } and then the [rum]{ ing="light-rum" }
1. Refrigerate, uncovered, for 1 hour to dispel the eggy taste
1. Whisking constantly, add the [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" } or half-and-half, cognac and [orange liqueur]{ ing="orange-liqueur" }
1. Refrigerate, covered, for at least 3 hours
1. Serve, garnishing each cup with freshly [grated nutmeg]{ ing="grated-nutmeg" }

## Notes

1. See the [original recipe](https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/voraciously/wp/2019/12/11/a-luxurious-and-strong-eggnog-recipe-to-sustain-you-through-this-holiday-season-and-many-more) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20210514174134/https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/voraciously/wp/2019/12/11/a-luxurious-and-strong-eggnog-recipe-to-sustain-you-through-this-holiday-season-and-many-more)) for a cooked variant
